module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.MeromorphicSectionTensorAffine

/-!
# The global product of two meromorphic sections

Let `X` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` satisfying the hypotheses (a) and (b) of
Stacks 0EN6, let `ℒ` and `𝒩` be quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-modules and let `s` and `t` be meromorphic
sections of `ℒ` and of `𝒩`.  Over an *affine* étale chart `s` and `t` are honest meromorphic
sections before sheafification and their chartwise product
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.meromorphicSectionTensorMul` is a section of `𝒦_X(ℒ ⊗ 𝒩)` with no
choices made; this file amalgamates those products into a **global** meromorphic section
`s ⊗ t` of `ℒ ⊗ 𝒪_X 𝒩`, the algebraic-space analogue of the product of Stacks 02SL.

The construction is in two steps, and both are governed by one property of a section of
`𝒦_X(ℒ ⊗ 𝒩)` over a chart `V`: that it restricts to the chartwise product over *every* affine
chart over `V`.  That property determines the section (the affine charts over `V` cover it) and
is inherited by restrictions, so the sections it picks out over the several charts are
automatically compatible and amalgamate to a global section by
`CategoryTheory.PresheafOfModules.sectionsMk`.

Existence over a single chart is the sheaf condition over the covering sieve generated by *all*
affine charts over it: the chartwise products attached to two of them agree over any common
refinement, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.map_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_meromorphicSectionTensorMul_eq`, which is
the compatibility the amalgamation consumes.  Taking all affine charts over `V` as the generating
family, rather than one covering family of them, is what makes the resulting section restrict
correctly over every affine chart and not merely over the chosen ones.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsChartwiseTensorMul`: the property above, of a section of
  `𝒦_X(ℒ ⊗ 𝒩)` over a chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.meromorphicSectionTensor`: the global product `s ⊗ t`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isChartwiseTensorMul`: existence over one chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsChartwiseTensorMul.eq`: the property determines the section.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsChartwiseTensorMul.restrict`: it is inherited by restrictions.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isChartwiseTensorMul_meromorphicSectionTensor`: the global product has
  the property over every chart, which is the formula computing it.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.eval_meromorphicSectionTensor_of_isAffine`: the value of the global
  product over an affine chart is the chartwise product of the representatives there.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EN5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EN5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EN6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EN6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02SL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02SL)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    {X : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (hX : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS X)
    (hwa : ∀ z ∈ weaklyAssociatedPointsOfSpace B S hS (⟨X, hX⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS),
      localRingDimension B S hS z = 0)
    (hfin : HasLocallyFiniteIrreducibleComponents B S hS X)
    (L N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X hX)
    (s : MeromorphicSection.{u, u} B S hS X hX L)
    (t : MeromorphicSection.{u, u} B S hS X hX N)

/-- **The property that determines the product of two meromorphic sections over a chart.**  A
section `p` of `𝒦_X(ℒ ⊗ 𝒩)` over a chart `V` has it when, over every *affine* chart `W` over `V`
and for every pair of representatives `x` of `s` and `y` of `t` there, the restriction of `p` to
`W` is the chartwise product
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.meromorphicSectionTensorMul` of `x` and `y`.

Over an affine chart the representatives exist and are unique (the module analogue of Stacks
0EN6 part (2)), so this says that `p` is the product wherever the product can be written down;
the affine charts over `V` cover it, so there is at most one such `p`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsChartwiseTensorMul.eq`). -/
def IsChartwiseTensorMul (V : SmallEtale B S hS X)
    (p : (meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
      (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val.obj (op V)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (W : SmallEtale B S hS X) (g : W ⟶ V), IsAffine (smallEtaleScheme B S hS X W) →
    ∀ (x : (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX L).obj (op W))
      (y : (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX N).obj (op W)),
      s.eval (op W) = toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX L W x →
      t.eval (op W) = toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX N W y →
      ((meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
            (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val.map g.op).hom p =
        toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N) W
          (meromorphicSectionTensorMul B S hS hX L N W x y)

include hwa hfin in
/-- **The product over a chart is determined by its restrictions to the affine charts over
it.**  The affine charts over a chart cover it
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.exists_affine_etale_ofArrows`), over each of them both
sections restrict to the chartwise product of the representatives there, and the sheaf
`𝒦_X(ℒ ⊗ 𝒩)` is separated
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.meromorphicSectionSheaf_eq_of_cover`). -/
theorem IsChartwiseTensorMul.eq (hLqc : L.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) (hNqc : N.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (V : SmallEtale B S hS X)
    {p q : (meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
      (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val.obj (op V)}
    (hp : IsChartwiseTensorMul B S hS hX L N s t V p)
    (hq : IsChartwiseTensorMul B S hS hX L N s t V q) :
    p = q := by
  obtain ⟨I, Y, a, hYaff, hcov, -⟩ := SmallEtale.exists_affine_etale_ofArrows B S hS X V
  refine meromorphicSectionSheaf_eq_of_cover B S hS X hX (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N) V
    Y a hcov p q fun i ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := exists_eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_of_isAffine B S hS hX hwa hfin
    L hLqc s (Y i) (hYaff i)
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := exists_eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_of_isAffine B S hS hX hwa hfin
    N hNqc t (Y i) (hYaff i)
  exact (hp (Y i) (a i) (hYaff i) x y hx hy).trans
    (hq (Y i) (a i) (hYaff i) x y hx hy).symm

/-- **The property is inherited by restrictions.**  An affine chart over a chart `V'` over `V` is
an affine chart over `V`, and restricting to it in two steps is restricting to it. -/
theorem IsChartwiseTensorMul.restrict (V V' : SmallEtale B S hS X) (k : V' ⟶ V)
    {p : (meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
      (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val.obj (op V)}
    (hp : IsChartwiseTensorMul B S hS hX L N s t V p) :
    IsChartwiseTensorMul B S hS hX L N s t V'
      (((meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
        (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val.map k.op).hom p) := by
  intro W g hW x y hx hy
  refine Eq.trans (PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply
    (meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
      (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val k.op g.op p).symm ?_
  exact hp W (g ≫ k) hW x y hx hy

include hwa hfin in
/-- **The product of two meromorphic sections exists over every chart.**  The covering sieve of
the chart generated by *all* the affine charts over it carries the chartwise products, which
agree over any common refinement
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.map_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_meromorphicSectionTensorMul_eq`), so the
sheaf condition for `𝒦_X(ℒ ⊗ 𝒩)` amalgamates them.

The generating family is all affine charts over `V` and not one covering family of them: that is
what makes the amalgamation restrict to the chartwise product over *every* affine chart over `V`,
which is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsChartwiseTensorMul`.  Over an affine chart `W` over `V` the
restriction of the amalgamation is the product attached to the chart the sieve factors `W`
through, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_meromorphicSectionTensorMul_restrict` — whose
affineness hypothesis is on the smaller chart, which is `W` — identifies it with the product
over `W`. -/
theorem exists_isChartwiseTensorMul (hLqc : L.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (hNqc : N.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) (V : SmallEtale B S hS X) :
    ∃ p : (meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
      (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val.obj (op V),
      IsChartwiseTensorMul B S hS hX L N s t V p := by
  classical
  set T : Sieve V := Sieve.ofArrows
    (fun i : Σ W : SmallEtale B S hS X,
      {g : W ⟶ V // IsAffine (smallEtaleScheme B S hS X W)} ↦ i.1)
    (fun i ↦ i.2.1)
  have hT : T ∈ SmallEtale.topology B S hS X V := by
    obtain ⟨I, Y, a, hYaff, hcov, -⟩ := SmallEtale.exists_affine_etale_ofArrows B S hS X V
    refine (SmallEtale.topology B S hS X).superset_covering ?_ hcov
    intro Z g hg
    obtain ⟨i, h, rfl⟩ := (Sieve.mem_ofArrows_iff Y a g).1 hg
    exact T.downward_closed (Sieve.ofArrows_mk _ _ ⟨Y i, a i, hYaff i⟩) h
  -- the representatives over each affine chart over `V`
  have hrep : ∀ i : Σ W : SmallEtale B S hS X,
      {g : W ⟶ V // IsAffine (smallEtaleScheme B S hS X W)},
      ∃ xy : (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX L).obj (op i.1) ×
        (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX N).obj (op i.1),
        s.eval (op i.1) = toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX L i.1 xy.1 ∧
          t.eval (op i.1) = toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX N i.1 xy.2 := by
    intro i
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := exists_eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_of_isAffine B S hS hX hwa hfin
      L hLqc s i.1 i.2.2
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := exists_eval_eq_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_of_isAffine B S hS hX hwa hfin
      N hNqc t i.1 i.2.2
    exact ⟨⟨x, y⟩, hx, hy⟩
  set P : (i : Σ W : SmallEtale B S hS X,
      {g : W ⟶ V // IsAffine (smallEtaleScheme B S hS X W)}) →
      (meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
        (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val.obj (op i.1) :=
    fun i ↦ toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N) i.1
      (meromorphicSectionTensorMul B S hS hX L N i.1 (hrep i).choose.1 (hrep i).choose.2)
  -- the products attached to two affine charts over `V` agree over any common refinement
  have hagree : ∀ (i j : Σ W : SmallEtale B S hS X,
        {g : W ⟶ V // IsAffine (smallEtaleScheme B S hS X W)})
      (Z : SmallEtale B S hS X) (k₁ : Z ⟶ i.1) (k₂ : Z ⟶ j.1),
      ((meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
            (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val.map k₁.op).hom (P i) =
        ((meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
            (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val.map k₂.op).hom (P j) := by
    intro i j Z k₁ k₂
    exact map_toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_meromorphicSectionTensorMul_eq B S hS hX hwa hfin L N
      hLqc hNqc s t i.1 j.1 Z k₁ k₂ (hrep i).choose.1 (hrep i).choose.2
      (hrep j).choose.1 (hrep j).choose.2 (hrep i).choose_spec.1 (hrep i).choose_spec.2
      (hrep j).choose_spec.1 (hrep j).choose_spec.2
  -- the sheaf condition for the underlying type-valued presheaf over `T`
  have hsh := (isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type (SmallEtale.topology B S hS X)
      ((meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
        (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val.presheaf ⋙ forget AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})).mp
    (Presheaf.isSheaf_comp_of_isSheaf (SmallEtale.topology B S hS X)
      (meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
        (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val.presheaf (forget AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})
      (meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
        (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).isSheaf) T hT
  set fam : Presieve.FamilyOfElements
      ((meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
        (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val.presheaf ⋙ forget AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})
      (T : Presieve V) :=
    fun Z g hg ↦ ((meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
        (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val.map (Sieve.ofArrows.h hg).op).hom
      (P (Sieve.ofArrows.i hg))
  have hcomp : fam.Compatible := by
    intro Z₁ Z₂ W e₁ e₂ g₁ g₂ h₁ h₂ _
    refine Eq.trans (PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply
      (meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
        (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val (Sieve.ofArrows.h h₁).op e₁.op _).symm ?_
    refine Eq.trans (hagree (Sieve.ofArrows.i h₁) (Sieve.ofArrows.i h₂) W
      (e₁ ≫ Sieve.ofArrows.h h₁) (e₂ ≫ Sieve.ofArrows.h h₂)) ?_
    exact PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply
      (meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
        (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val (Sieve.ofArrows.h h₂).op e₂.op _
  refine ⟨hsh.amalgamate fam hcomp, ?_⟩
  intro W g hW x y hx hy
  have hg : T g := Sieve.ofArrows_mk _ _ (⟨W, g, hW⟩ :
    Σ W : SmallEtale B S hS X, {g : W ⟶ V // IsAffine (smallEtaleScheme B S hS X W)})
  refine Eq.trans (hsh.valid_glue hcomp g hg) ?_
  exact toMeromorphicSectionSheaf_meromorphicSectionTensorMul_restrict B S hS hX hwa hfin L N
    hLqc hNqc s t (Sieve.ofArrows.i hg).1 W hW (Sieve.ofArrows.h hg)
    (hrep (Sieve.ofArrows.i hg)).choose.1 (hrep (Sieve.ofArrows.i hg)).choose.2 x y
    (hrep (Sieve.ofArrows.i hg)).choose_spec.1 (hrep (Sieve.ofArrows.i hg)).choose_spec.2 hx hy

include hwa hfin in
/-- **The product of two meromorphic sections**, the algebraic-space analogue of the product of
Stacks 02SL: the global meromorphic section of `ℒ ⊗_{𝒪_X} 𝒩` whose restriction to every affine
chart is the chartwise product
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.meromorphicSectionTensorMul` of the representatives of `s` and of `t`
there.

The value over a chart is the section `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isChartwiseTensorMul`
produces, and compatibility with restriction is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsChartwiseTensorMul.restrict` followed by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsChartwiseTensorMul.eq`: the restriction of the value over `V` has the
property over `V'`, and so does the value over `V'`, and the property determines the section. -/
def meromorphicSectionTensor (hLqc : L.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (hNqc : N.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) :
    MeromorphicSection.{u, u} B S hS X hX (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N) :=
  PresheafOfModules.sectionsMk
    (fun U ↦ (exists_isChartwiseTensorMul B S hS hX hwa hfin L N s t hLqc hNqc U.unop).choose)
    (fun U U' f ↦ IsChartwiseTensorMul.eq B S hS hX hwa hfin L N s t hLqc hNqc U'.unop
      (IsChartwiseTensorMul.restrict B S hS hX L N s t U.unop U'.unop f.unop
        (exists_isChartwiseTensorMul B S hS hX hwa hfin L N s t hLqc hNqc U.unop).choose_spec)
      (exists_isChartwiseTensorMul B S hS hX hwa hfin L N s t hLqc hNqc U'.unop).choose_spec)

include hwa hfin in
/-- **The product of two meromorphic sections restricts to the chartwise product over every
affine chart.**  This is the formula that computes
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.meromorphicSectionTensor`, and the property that characterizes it. -/
theorem isChartwiseTensorMul_meromorphicSectionTensor (hLqc : L.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (hNqc : N.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) (V : SmallEtale B S hS X) :
    IsChartwiseTensorMul B S hS hX L N s t V
      ((meromorphicSectionTensor B S hS hX hwa hfin L N s t hLqc hNqc).eval (op V)) :=
  (exists_isChartwiseTensorMul B S hS hX hwa hfin L N s t hLqc hNqc V).choose_spec

include hwa hfin in
/-- **The value of the product over an affine chart is the chartwise product.**  Over an affine
chart `V` the meromorphic sections `s` and `t` have representatives `x` and `y`, and the value of
`s ⊗ t` there is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.meromorphicSectionTensorMul` of the two. -/
theorem eval_meromorphicSectionTensor_of_isAffine (hLqc : L.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (hNqc : N.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) (V : SmallEtale B S hS X)
    (hV : IsAffine (smallEtaleScheme B S hS X V))
    (x : (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX L).obj (op V))
    (y : (meromorphicSectionModule B S hS X hX N).obj (op V))
    (hx : s.eval (op V) = toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX L V x)
    (hy : t.eval (op V) = toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX N V y) :
    (meromorphicSectionTensor B S hS hX hwa hfin L N s t hLqc hNqc).eval (op V) =
      toMeromorphicSectionSheaf B S hS X hX (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N) V
        (meromorphicSectionTensorMul B S hS hX L N V x y) := by
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (isChartwiseTensorMul_meromorphicSectionTensor B S hS hX hwa hfin L N s t
    hLqc hNqc V V (𝟙 V) hV x y hx hy)
  exact (PresheafOfModules.sections_property
    (M := (meromorphicSectionSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX
      (picardTensorModule B S hS hX L N)).val)
    (meromorphicSectionTensor B S hS hX hwa hfin L N s t hLqc hNqc) (𝟙 (op V))).symm

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
